# A file directive's path with a character that is not ASCII can only be
# written percent-encoded: the compiler and bless refuse a url with the
# character as it is, and a browser sends the path encoded, which the
# runtime compares with the directives as written.  So the page's src, the
# directive and the lookup have the same spelling, and match.  The image is
# named by the path's last segment as written.
mode=accept
tls=none
form=(From=alice@example.com To=bob@example.net Subject=Logo Body=$'Plain text\n' Html=world Srcs=/caf%C3%A9.png User=alice Password=secret)
